& [SourceShapeFixtureFault]
  + the first focused test looked for SemanticUnit and PreparedRuntime as plus-marker attribute clauses
  + the governed SOP declares both as ampersand-marker subjects while Cantor is a plus-marker attribute
  + the test failed before projection the exact prefixes were corrected and both focused tests passed

& [GlobalEvidenceOrderingFault]
  + the first full-workspace run began after README changed but before transitive evidence manifests were rehashed
  + all product tests reached by that point including both new tests passed and the run stopped on the expected README size mismatch evidence gate
  + completion reruns the workspace only after final documentation and dependency-first manifest refresh

& [WSLPathInvocationFault]
  + the first full-workspace command allowed host shell expansion to inject a Windows PATH containing unquoted parentheses into bash
  + bash refused before Cargo started
  + the rerun used an explicit bounded WSL-native PATH and an ephemeral python-to-python3 fixture shim

& [EphemeralShimLifetimeFault]
  + a later workspace invocation assumed the temporary shim still existed but the WSL temporary directory had been discarded between invocations
  + five existing attention-MCP fixtures failed before product execution because command python was absent
  + final verification creates the alias in the same bash process that launches Cargo and removes it afterward

& [ColdTimeoutFixtureFault]
  + one existing 150-millisecond route-timeout fixture returned an adapter error during a cold heavily compiling workspace pass
  + its exact isolated rerun passed and the complete warm serialized workspace rerun also passed without changing timeout code or policy
  + this is retained as host timing evidence rather than hidden or converted into a product relaxation

& [SecurityDisposition]
